<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Büyük Süleyman Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1802</span> · Also known as Sulayman the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Büyük Süleyman Pasha, 'Sulayman the Great', was a Georgian-born mamluk who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> from 1780 to 1802, the high point of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. He restored order, enlarged the slave-soldier household and fought Persian incursions, Arab tribes and Wahhabi raiders. The Baban emir Ibrahim Pasha named his new capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulaymaniyah">Sulaymaniyah</a>, after him in 1784.</p></div>
